# Optional overrides for the SPA's API target (src/api/client.ts).
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) only if you need to change the defaults.
#
# DEFAULT (no .env needed): every build — `npm run dev` AND `npm run build` —
# talks to the real backend at the relative path `/api`. In dev, vite.config.ts
# ships a `server.proxy` that forwards /api/* to Flask on localhost:5000; in
# prod, Flask serves the SPA same-origin. If no backend is running, the app
# fails LOUDLY with a "Can't reach the backend API" error — it never silently
# falls back to fake data.
#
# Backend on a different host/port (bypass the dev proxy)? Point at it:
# VITE_API_BASE=http://localhost:5000/api
#
# Want the offline demo (seeded sample transcript/programs/GPA, nothing real)?
# Opt in explicitly — a persistent "Demo data" banner will remind you
# (frontend/src/layouts/AppLayout.tsx):
# VITE_API_BASE=mock
#
# Note: this is a DEV-ONLY setting. Vite inlines env vars at build time, so
# leaving it here would bake sample data into a deployable bundle — vite.config.ts
# fails `npm run build` while it's set (override: ALLOW_MOCK_BUILD=1).
